  partName: Oil Pan Bolt
  description: The Oil Pan Bolt is a tiny, complex-shaped component located at the
    bottom-left-front of the engine, made of Material.001, and is responsible for
    securing the oil pan to the engine block. Its primary function is to prevent
    oil leaks and maintain the integrity of the engine's lubrication system, and
    its material composition provides the necessary strength and corrosion resistance.
    Notably, the Oil Pan Bolt is often designed with a specialized thread pattern
    or coating to enhance its sealing properties and prevent damage from oil and
    other contaminants.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
